    "related_formalizations": [
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4 (Matrix.det, Matrix.det_succ_row_zero, Matrix.det_submatrix_equiv_self, Matrix.charpoly, Hermitian matrices, Polynomial.reverse/reflect, intermediate value theorem, sSup/compactness, monotone convergence)",
        "note": "Uses Mathlib's determinant, polynomial, topology, order and Hermitian-matrix APIs. The Coxeter-element determinant bridge, star-tree determinant recurrence, spectral bound and limit proofs are provided by this repository; its CoxElt module is inherited from the related Mahler repository as recorded below.",
        "relationship": "builds-on"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "Registered entry PALOMAR-2026-09-01-000005 (https://github.com/stalex444/mahler-minimizer-compositum), version 2 revision 84b364a5f98daefc1be387ae0aeb3d39866eca79",
        "note": "Registered version 2's compared statements (18), (20) and (21) concern E_m = T(2,3,m-3). (18) is the Coxeter polynomial identity for m >= 4; (1) here at (p,q) = (2,3), m = r + 3, is its m >= 5 case, with the same node labelling and right-hand side: F_{2,3} = X^3 - X - 1 and F* = 1 - X^2 - X^3. Together, (20) and (21) imply (3) here at (2,3): (20) gives increase to the plastic number with the stronger threshold m >= 10 (r >= 7) and lower bound 117/100, and (21) gives spectral dominance. This package extends the formula and spectral limit to each fixed (p,q). The unregistered proposal at revision 1a85306b04fb78a47ea5526c840105b46eec7a32 selected the D_n = T(2,2,n-2) formula and a unit-circle corollary. The revised version 3 candidate at ab5420bce3edf3182a5216c22a81d40731edd8b9 instead selects 25 statements, adding cyclotomic classification and Salem minimal-polynomial results; the mirror/D_n material is auxiliary. Neither candidate is identified here as a registered version. These special cases are disclosed overlap. The inherited CoxElt module is that entry's Coxeter-element module, byte-identical apart from the file name in the baseline version (SHA-256 recorded in BUILD.txt).",
        "relationship": "other"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "Registered entry PALOMAR-2026-10-17-000013 (https://github.com/stalex444/triangle-group-growth, commit 874b6a2)",
        "note": "Growth series of the triangle Coxeter groups (p,q,inf). It proves, for (p,q) != (2,2), a unique tau(p,q) > 1 with (tau^-1 + ... + tau^-(p-1))(tau^-1 + ... + tau^-(q-1)) = 1, tau strictly increasing in (p,q), rho <= tau with equality exactly at (2,3) and (3,2), tau < 2 and tau -> 2. That entry kernel-holds that this is the growth-rate equation of (p,q,inf); this package does not. Compared statement (4) proves only that F_{p,q}(tau) = 0 and that equation are equivalent for tau > 0, so L(p,q) = tau(p,q). Through (4), compared statements (2) and (5) RESTATE that entry's uniqueness, tau < 2 and \"rho <= tau, equality exactly at (2,3)\": they are re-proved and compared here in the star-ladder form so that this package is self-contained, with the overlap disclosed, and are not claimed as new. The objects differ: that entry is about growth series of triangle groups, this one about Coxeter elements of star trees.",
        "relationship": "other"
      }
